% WildfireGuardian project bibliography
% Created and checked: 2026-10-08 (Asia/Seoul).
%
% Scope: the current maintained wildfire_burned_area_hourly and expected_heat_flux
% workflow, retained publisher reconstruction code/data, and clearly marked
% mathematical or historical background. Absent legacy applications are excluded.
%
% Entries use conventional BibTeX types, including misc for datasets/software,
% for compatibility with BibTeX and biblatex. No guessed DOI, release date, or
% individual author is assigned where the available sources do not support one.
% Web access dates identify consultation, not publication or data acquisition.
% Software paper years identify publications, not the installed package release.
% Primary-source metadata access and full-text inspection are different checks.
% Entry-specific roles and verification boundaries are recorded in the companion
% wildfire_references_audit.json. keywords and annotation fields can be used by
% biblatex or reference managers; traditional BibTeX generally ignores them.
%
% Example (main .tex and this .bib in the same directory):
%   \usepackage[numbers]{natbib}
%   \usepackage{url}
%   ...
%   \cite{choi2026wildfiretoa,toadeposit}
%   \bibliographystyle{plainnat}
%   \bibliography{wildfire_references}
% Use \nocite{*} only when the intention is to print this complete inventory.
%
% The existing wildfire_methods.tex uses an inline thebibliography environment.
% To migrate it, replace that environment with the two bibliography commands and
% load a suitable citation package. Most existing keys are retained. Its combined
% heatrefs item must be replaced by the three separate keys:
%   overholt2014, angelidis2004, vanoosterom1983.
% The article choi2026wildfiretoa and dataset toadeposit are separate works.
%

